⛔⛔ INSTRUMENT LESSON OF RECORD: THE uuid ROTATED (6f748ddc -> 3acfe9c4) AND THE OLD uuid KEPT SERVING THE 8/21 FILE AT HTTP 200, so BOTH hash monitors reported 'unchanged' forever and NEITHER FIRED. The PICKER found it. RUN THE PICKER FIRST, ALWAYS. ⛔ AND THE 588 OVERVIEW-TOTAL TRIGGER I ADDED THIS MORNING IS REFUTED: the total is STILL 588 because gas +5 offset oil -5 — a FALSE NEGATIVE. My own perimeter rule (total != oil leg) bit the trigger I built on the total; IT CUTS BOTH WAYS. DO NOT REUSE THE TOTAL AS A PRINT-DETECTOR. || ⚑ URL RE-DISCOVERY, SOLVED AND TESTED (added 2026-08-28 11:4x — my earlier 'RE-DISCOVER THE REPORT URL' said WHAT to do and not HOW, which is the same incomplete-handoff defect I had already committed once today). THE INDEX PAGE IS https://rigcount.bakerhughes.com/na-rig-count -- it lists 10 static-file uuids INCLUDING the current report AND `e98bcf83`, THE ARCHIVE FILE THAT COST THIS DESK A MONTH ON 8/14 (it serves `08-29-2025 North America Rig Count Report.xlsx`, A YEAR STALE, and BOTH link texts contain the words 'New Report'). ⛔ SO NEVER PICK BY LINK TEXT. PICK BY THE DATE IN `content-disposition`, which is unambiguous and cannot be fooled by the link text. HEAD requests only -- no 8MB downloads. RECIPE (verified in this exact form 2026-08-28 11:4x; returned `08-21-2026 North_America Rig_Count Report.xlsx` and CONFIRMED the registry probe 6f748ddc is still current): python3 -c "import urllib.request,re;U={'User-Agent':'Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/126.0 Safari/537.36','Cache-Control':'no-cache'};C=type('H',(urllib.request.Request,),{'get_method':lambda s:'HEAD'});h=urllib.request.urlopen(urllib.request.Request('https://rigcount.bakerhughes.com/na-rig-count',headers=U),timeout=60).read().decode('utf-8','replace');b=None
for i in sorted(set(re.findall(r'static-files/([0-9a-f-]{36})',h))):
 try:cd=(urllib.request.urlopen(C('https://rigcount.bakerhughes.com/static-files/'+i,headers=U),timeout=45).headers.get('content-disposition') or '')
 except Exception:continue
 m=re.search(r'(\d{2})-(\d{2})-(\d{4})\s+North[_ ]America\s+Rig[_ ]Count\s+Report\.xlsx',cd,re.I)
 if m:
  k=(m.group(3),m.group(1),m.group(2))
  if b is None or k>b[0]:b=(k,i,m.group(0))
print(b[2],'https://rigcount.bakerhughes.com/static-files/'+b[1])" ★ RUN THIS FIRST AT EVERY GRADE, NOT ONLY ON A SILENT MONITOR: it costs 11 HEADs, it names the report DATE so you cannot grade a stale file, and it SELF-VALIDATES the registry probe every time. || ⚑ SECOND, UUID-INDEPENDENT 'HAS THE WEEK PRINTED?' SIGNAL (added 2026-08-28 11:4x). RISK IT COVERS: both the BRENT and PROME monitors watch the sha256 at static-file 6f748ddc. THAT URL UPDATING IN PLACE EACH WEEK IS AN UNTESTED ASSUMPTION — n=0 observed transitions through it, and this desk has already been burned once by BH serving two different static-files whose link texts BOTH read 'New Report' (the 8/14 archive-file mis-pick). If BH mints a NEW uuid instead of replacing the file, BOTH hash-monitors stay SILENT FOREVER and the guard reads 'not up yet' indefinitely. THE INDEPENDENT SIGNAL: https://rigcount.bakerhughes.com/rig-count-overview carries the US TOTAL in-page. It reads 588 right now = the 8/21 total (452 oil + 127 gas + 9 misc, reproduced at the 8/21 grade). WHEN 588 CHANGES, THE WEEK HAS PRINTED — whatever the static-file does. CHECK: .venv/bin/python3 -c "import urllib.request,re; h=urllib.request.urlopen(urllib.request.Request('https://rigcount.bakerhughes.com/rig-count-overview',headers={'User-Agent':'Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/126.0 Safari/537.36'}),timeout=60).read().decode('utf-8','replace'); print(sorted(set(re.findall(r' 5[89][0-9] ',h))))" -- VERIFIED IN THIS FORM 2026-08-28 11:4x, returns ['588']. ⛔⛔ TRIGGER ONLY, NEVER A GRADE SOURCE: the overview publishes the US TOTAL and THE TOTAL IS NOT A PROXY FOR THE OIL LEG (8/14: total +5 while oil +1). Confusing the two is this row's live perimeter trap. If the total moves and the static-file hash does NOT, the uuid rotated -- RE-DISCOVER THE REPORT URL, do not grade off the total. || PENDING at 11:0x ET, NOT PRE-GRADED. Two standing instrument caveats, both measured: (1) the BH host TARPITS a self-identifying User-Agent — use a browser UA (the 8/21 repair; instrument_check probed CLEAN at this boot); (2) NEVER grade off a digit-regex on the BH HTML — it returns `457`, this row's own level, out of Drupal CSS/UUID fragments. LESSONS #1: two independent pulls. DO NOT LET GRADES STACK.
